Wave Workbench @PROJECT_VERSION@ - Windows x64 portable package

Desktop application
  wave-workbench.exe

Primary automation entry point
  wave-cli.exe capabilities --pretty
  wave-cli.exe --help

Compatibility tools
  wave-cli.exe generate <wave-generate arguments...>
  wave-cli.exe compare <wave-compare arguments...>
  wave-cli.exe bridge <wave-bridge arguments...>

Experimental simulation runner
  wave-sim-runner.exe --help
  wave-sim-runner.exe probe --pretty
  The fixed-fixture path consumes Module Manifest and Stimulus Scenario
  contracts. It is not connected to the desktop UI yet.

The legacy wave-generate.exe, wave-compare.exe and wave-bridge.exe entry points
remain installed for existing scripts. The wave-cli compatibility adapters
forward their arguments, text output and exit codes without translation.

Documentation
  docs\cli-quick-start.md
  docs\automation-cli.md
  docs\integration-contracts.md
  docs\simulation-runner.md
  docs\project-format.md

Minimal operation example
  docs\examples\quick-start.operations.json

Machine-readable JSON Schemas
  schemas\automation\v1\capabilities.schema.json
  schemas\automation\v1\report.schema.json
  schemas\automation\v1\operation-batch.schema.json

Example project
  examples\handshake\project.wave.json

Requirements
  64-bit Windows 10 or Windows 11. Installation is not required.
  Qt and compiler runtime libraries were collected by windeployqt when this
  package was generated from the source repository.

On-demand FST reader
  wave-wellen-reader.exe
  FST metadata is indexed first; transition data is decoded only for selected
  or mapped signals. See docs\fst-reader.md for limits and attribution.
